  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The new streaming video player appears to conflict with user A/v codex and be dependent of features in the operating system. For example windows 7 users may not be able to see or hear the video well most windows 10 and 8 users will not.    I am a win 7 user and have consistent playback problems with this new stream player.\nI have playback  issues from crashing to no audio depending on what codex pack i install in my windows 7.  I use the k-light codex pack, and currently i can only see video and not hear it. Out of date versions of this codex pack may crash me as a enter the room, which was resolved by updating to recent version 14.2.5.\nI have found a hint in the error log that may explain support issues and recommend the codex be tested and a guide to provide compatibility with windows 7.\n.\n.\n.\n[Warning:7/1/2018 11:43:05 PM] [AVProVideo] If video fails to play then it may be due to the resolution being higher than 1920x1080 which is the limitation of the Microsoft DirectShow H.264 decoder.\nTo resolve this you can either use Windows 8 or above (and disable 'Force DirectShow' option), resize your video, use a different codec (such as Hap or DivX), or install a 3rd party H.264 decoder such as LAV Filters.",
